      "id": "claim_9ea932e4b4db4069b2dd05dc6d5eb153",
      "statement": "Every application message is a WebSocketEnvelope with type 'message', optional id, optional target (browserInstanceId and tabId), and an unknown typed payload; BrijioEnvelope is an alias. Relay-level rejections use a separate BrijioErrorEnvelope with type 'error'.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/shared/src/protocol.ts#L1-L9",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c9fb1e4cd894affcdecc4553117783ac2c2770cc4460941a1bd42260086a4201:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://packages/shared/src/protocol.ts#L364-L371",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e5702164de153076ab7deab10c4b1ca4460e926aa8af54927b3854835371af63:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1844d5b0c45247b99dbdd0c3a940bc58",
      "statement": "The relay parses each incoming frame with parseBrijioEnvelope, which JSON.parses and validates type 'message' plus a payload property; invalid JSON yields invalid_json and a non-envelope yields invalid_message, both as BrijioErrorEnvelope.",
