      "id": "claim_803df2d12c24440c82a226a89e404bd0",
      "statement": "TabInfo carries opaque tabId and windowId as strings (raw Chrome/Safari ids as strings, so the shape can transition to opaque UUIDs for the cloud model without a protocol change), plus title, url (HTTP/HTTPS only), active, and supported (always true for listed tabs). Tab list responses use payload type 'tab_list_response' with ok true/false.",
